Z||000000||BAM-BAM||11-02-2000||12:09 AM||||  If, I were to get a set of wheels that were 17x7.5 5-100mm with a +35mm offset, what could I do to make them work on my 85GT that has been lowered using Eibach springs without scrubbing? Please tell me that there exists a spacer or something that will make these work. If not, then I am forced to go with a TSW BIG DEEP or the Konig Toxxins. MOMO doesn't make anything in a 40+ offset. TIA and LMK.<P> Thank, Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||11-02-2000||01:14 AM||||5mm spacers should work fine.. don't know where to get any, tho.  Shouldn't be too hard to have a machine shop make a set out of aluminum..  and a 5mm spacer shouldn't be big enough to put any undue stress on anything..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||11-02-2000||07:42 AM||||  Cool, correct me if I'm wrong; I am also doing the GA/Baretta brake upgrade and to my understanding, this puts the wheel out another 9mm anyway. With this applcation, should I still need a spacer? Or would tha 9mm be sufficient? I think that If I spaced it out to far it would look funny. Let me know guys/gals, I'm still learning. These are the things that others will want to know in the future. Also, I shouldn't have to worry at all about the rear correct? Or, how about this; GA/Baretta brakes up front and spacer in the rear? Now I feel a since of calm. I may E-Mail some of you for advice.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000003||stsmithgt||11-02-2000||10:18 AM||||35mm + 9mm = 44mm.....Hmmm, You need a -4mm anti-spacer.  They sell those at the anti-auto parts store. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR> (geez my humor sucks)||||reg||1
